  "summary": "临床语言学是应用语言学的一个分支，研究各类沟通障碍者的语言行为，并把语言学的理论与描写方法用于评估、诊断和干预。它借助音系学、形态句法学、语义学和语用学的分析工具，刻画失语症、发展性语言障碍、构音障碍、口吃等表现，为言语-语言病理学提供理论依据。语料主要来自自然会话、标准化测验和实验任务，强调描写的精确、可量化与可复现。",
  "summaryEn": "Clinical linguistics is the branch of applied linguistics that studies the language behaviour of people with communication disorders and applies linguistic theory and description to assessment, diagnosis and intervention. Drawing on phonology, morphosyntax, semantics and pragmatics, it characterises conditions such as aphasia, developmental language disorder, dysarthria and stuttering. Data come from spontaneous conversation, standardised tests and experimental tasks, and analysis stresses descriptive precision, quantification and replicability.",
