  "summaryEn": "Psycholinguistics investigates the psychological mechanisms and cognitive processes underlying human language comprehension and production, asking how linguistic knowledge is represented and processed in real time and how children acquire language. It combines linguistics, cognitive psychology and experimental methods, using reaction times, eye movements and brain responses to reveal the regularities and constraints of language processing."
