  "summaryEn": "Neurolinguistics studies the relationship between language ability and the brain's neural mechanisms, examining how phonology, vocabulary and syntax are represented and processed in the brain. It combines clinical observation of aphasia, electrophysiological recording and functional brain imaging to test the roles of areas such as Broca's area and Wernicke's area in language processing, and interacts closely with psycholinguistics."
