  "summary": "符号学是研究符号、符号系统及其意义的学科，考察符号如何指代表达、如何被解释以及符号之间如何组合。索绪尔提出能指与所指的二元模式，皮尔士建立图像、指示与象征的三分法，莫里斯区分句法、语义与语用三个层面。符号学与语言学关系密切，却把语言视为更普遍的符号现象中的一类，其方法被广泛用于文学、影视、广告、建筑与文化分析。",
  "summaryEn": "Semiotics is the study of signs, sign systems and meaning: how signs stand for something, how they are interpreted, and how they combine with one another. Saussure proposed a two-part model of signifier and signified, Peirce distinguished icon, index and symbol, and Morris separated syntax, semantics and pragmatics. Closely tied to linguistics, semiotics treats language as one sign system among many, and its methods are applied to literature, film, advertising, architecture and culture at large.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": "定义与基本概念",
    "hEn": "Definition and Basic Concepts",
    "p": [
     "符号学源自希腊语 sēmeion，意为记号，研究符号的构成、运作与解释。符号通常被理解为以一物代指另一物的关系，须由三方面构成：可感知的形式、所传达的内容，以及使用者的解释。索绪尔把符号分为能指与所指，强调二者联结的任意性；皮尔士则把符号过程视为符号、对象与解释项的三元关系，认为解释本身又会产生新的符号。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Semiotics, from Greek sēmeion meaning sign, studies how signs are constituted, how they work and how they are interpreted. A sign is usually defined as something that stands for something else, and it involves a perceptible form, a conveyed content and an interpreter. Saussure divided the sign into signifier and signified, stressing the arbitrariness of their link, whereas Peirce treated semiosis as a triadic relation among sign, object and interpretant, in which every interpretation produces a further sign."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "主要理论与分类",
    "hEn": "Main Theories and Classifications",
    "p": [
     "皮尔士按符号与对象的关系分出三类：图像符号以相似性为基础，如肖像与地图；指示符号以因果或邻接关系为基础，如烟指示火、箭头指示方向；象征符号以约定俗成为基础，如汉语的书和英语的 book。莫里斯把符号学分为句法、语义与语用三支，分别处理符号之间的组合、符号与所指的关系以及符号与使用者的关系。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Peirce distinguished three kinds of sign by their relation to the object: icons, based on resemblance, such as a portrait or a map; indices, based on causal or contiguous connection, such as smoke indicating fire or an arrow indicating direction; and symbols, based on convention, such as Chinese shū or English book. Morris divided semiotics into syntax, semantics and pragmatics, dealing respectively with combinations among signs, signs and their referents, and signs and their users."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "示例与分析方法",
    "hEn": "Examples and Analytical Method",
    "p": [
     "符号学分析通常把日常现象拆解为相互对立的符号项。以交通信号为例，红灯与绿灯的意义来自同一系统内的对立，而非颜色本身；在语言中，汉语普通话的 /p/ 与 /pʰ/ 构成爸 [pa⁵¹] 与怕 [pʰa⁵¹] 的对立，同样说明价值由系统差异决定。罗兰·巴特进一步分析神话，指出能指与所指结合后可以整体再充当新的能指，从而承载文化意涵。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Semiotic analysis often decomposes everyday phenomena into opposed signifying items. In traffic lights, the meaning of red and green comes from a contrast within one system rather than from the colours themselves; in language, the contrast between Mandarin /p/ and /pʰ/ in 爸 [pa⁵¹] father and 怕 [pʰa⁵¹] to fear likewise shows that value depends on systemic difference. Roland Barthes extended this to myth, showing how a completed sign can serve as a new signifier carrying cultural connotations."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "与语言学的关系",
    "hEn": "Relation to Linguistics",
    "p": [
     "索绪尔把符号学设想为一门更一般的科学，语言学只是其中一部分；雅各布森与列维-斯特劳斯则把音位对立与二元对立的分析方法推向人类学与诗学。今天符号学与语用学、话语分析、社会语言学多有交叉，指示语研究就同时属于两门学科。批评者认为，符号学有时过于依赖直觉式的对立分析，缺乏可重复的验证程序。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Saussure envisaged semiotics as a general science of which linguistics would be one part, while Jakobson and Lévi-Strauss carried phonological and binary oppositional methods into anthropology and poetics. Today semiotics overlaps with pragmatics, discourse analysis and sociolinguistics; deixis, for instance, belongs to both fields. Critics argue that semiotic analysis sometimes relies on intuitive oppositions and lacks replicable procedures of verification."
    ]
   }
  ],
