  "summaryEn": "Pragmatics studies the relations between linguistic signs and their users and contexts, focusing on how speakers convey intentions beyond the literal meaning with the help of context, and how hearers infer those intentions. Its core topics include deixis, speech acts, implicature, presupposition and politeness, and it is closely connected with semantics, sociolinguistics and cognitive science."
