  "summary": "一致关系指句子中两个或更多成分在某些语法特征上相互呼应、必须保持相同的形态现象，典型如主语与谓语在人称、数、性上的一致。英语 He walks 中的 -s、德语 die gute Suppe 中冠词与形容词的呼应、斯瓦希里语中动词前缀与名词类别的配合都是实例。一致关系是形态学与句法学的交汇点，也是语言类型学比较与语言处理研究的重要参项。",
  "summaryEn": "Agreement is the phenomenon whereby two or more elements in a sentence covary in certain grammatical features, most typically person, number and gender between subject and predicate. English He walks with its -s ending, German die gute Suppe with matching article and adjective, and the noun-class prefixes cross-referenced on Swahili verbs are familiar instances. Agreement sits at the interface of morphology and syntax and is a major parameter in typology and processing research.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": "定义",
    "hEn": "Definition",
    "p": [
     "一致关系指句法上相关联的成分在性、数、人称、格、有定性等特征上保持一致的系统现象。其中一方为控制项，提供特征值，另一方为目标，通过屈折词尾或附着形式体现这些值。如英语 This book is interesting 与 These books are interesting 中，指示词、名词与动词 be 的数必须彼此匹配，说 This books are 则不合法。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Agreement is the systematic covariation of syntactically related elements in features such as gender, number, person, case and definiteness. One element, the controller, supplies the feature values, while the other, the target, realizes them through inflection or clitics. In English this book is interesting versus these books are interesting, the demonstrative, noun and verb must match in number; this books are is ungrammatical."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "研究内容与分类",
    "hEn": "Types and Dimensions",
    "p": [
     "研究者通常区分几种维度：按控制项分为主语一致、宾语一致与所有格一致；按目标分为动词一致、形容词一致与限定词一致；按范围分为完全一致与部分一致。班图语中的名词类别一致非常发达，一个名词类前缀会同时出现在形容词、数词和动词上，形成全句性的呼应网络，说话人必须追踪每个名词的类别才能正确屈折其余成分。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Several dimensions are usually distinguished: by controller, subject agreement, object agreement and possessor agreement; by target, verbal, adjectival and determiner agreement; by extent, full versus partial agreement. Noun-class agreement in Bantu languages is especially elaborate, since a class prefix recurs on adjectives, numerals and verbs, producing a sentence-wide network of cross-reference. Speakers must therefore track the class of every noun in order to inflect the rest of the clause correctly."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "示例",
    "hEn": "Examples",
    "p": [
     "拉丁语 puella bona est「这女孩是好的」中，名词、形容词与系词均为阴性单数；换成 puer bonus est 则全句转为阳性。西班牙语 los libros nuevos 与 la casa nueva 显示冠词与形容词随名词的性与数变化。日语「私は彼が来たと思う」中，从句主语用「が」，主句话题用「は」，体现另一层次的呼应。汉语缺乏严格意义的形态一致，主要依靠语序和虚词。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "In Latin puella bona est, the noun, adjective and copula are all feminine singular, whereas puer bonus est is masculine throughout. Spanish los libros nuevos versus la casa nueva shows the article and adjective shifting with the gender and number of the noun. Japanese uses ga for the subject of an embedded clause and wa for the matrix topic. Mandarin has no morphological agreement of this kind and relies on word order and function words."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "主要理论",
    "hEn": "Theoretical Accounts",
    "p": [
     "生成语法把一致视为句法核心功能语类（如 T 或早期的 Agr）上的特征核查与赋值过程，当前最简方案以特征继承和探针—目标关系解释一致。词汇功能语法用功能结构中的统一运算处理一致，构式语法与基于用法的研究则强调一致模式来自对具体构式的概括。心理语言学研究还显示，说话人对一致错误的敏感可在数百毫秒内显现。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Generative grammar treats agreement as feature checking and valuation in functional heads such as T or the older Agr node; in current Minimalism it follows from feature inheritance and the probe-goal relation. Lexical-functional grammar handles agreement through unification in functional structure, while construction grammar and usage-based approaches emphasize that agreement patterns are generalizations over concrete constructions. Processing studies additionally show that speakers are sensitive to agreement violations within milliseconds."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "争议与批评",
    "hEn": "Debates and Criticisms",
    "p": [
     "一致关系的争论包括：一致是纯句法现象还是形态现象；「部分一致」和「一致语素脱落」应当如何解释；以及英语、汉语是否真的缺少一致。有学者主张一致主要服务于语用上的指称识别，也有研究指出某些语言中一致仅部分实现，受生命度、语序和信息结构等条件制约。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Debates about agreement include whether it is purely syntactic or morphological, how partial agreement and agreement drop should be analysed, and whether languages such as English or Mandarin genuinely lack agreement. Some scholars argue that agreement mainly serves referential identification in discourse, while others show that in many languages agreement is realized only partially and is conditioned by animacy, word order and information structure."
    ]
   }
  ],
