  "summaryEn": "Conversational implicature is a core concept introduced by Grice: meaning that a speaker conveys beyond the literal content of an utterance and that the hearer infers on the basis of the Cooperative Principle and the context. It is calculable, cancellable and non-detachable, and divides into generalized and particularized implicature. It remains the central topic of research on pragmatic inference."
