  "summary": "命题是语义学中表示句子所表达的、可判定真假的抽象内容，它独立于具体语言形式与说话场合。同一命题可由不同句子表达，如英语 Snow is white 与汉语「雪是白的」在真值条件上等同。命题是信念、知道、断言等命题态度动词的宾语，也是逻辑推理与真值语义学的基本单位。自弗雷格以来，命题被视为超越语句与言语行为的第三层意义对象。",
  "summaryEn": "A proposition is the abstract, truth-evaluable content expressed by a sentence, independent of any particular language or occasion of use. Different sentences, such as English Snow is white and Chinese 「雪是白的」, may express the same proposition. Propositions serve as the objects of propositional-attitude verbs like believe and know, and as the basic units of truth-conditional semantics and logical inference. Since Frege they have been treated as a level of meaning distinct from sentences and utterances.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": "定义与基本特征",
    "hEn": "Definition and Basic Characteristics",
    "p": [
     "命题是语句所表达的抽象意义内容，其核心特征是可真可假。英语句子 The cat is on the mat 与汉语「猫在垫子上」形式迥异，却表达同一命题，因为二者在同一情形下同为真、同为假。命题既不是句子本身，也不是说话事件：同一句子在不同场合可以表达不同命题，如含指示语的「我明天来」随说话人与时间而变。真值条件因此成为判定命题同一性的基本标准。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "A proposition is the abstract content expressed by a sentence, and its defining feature is that it can be true or false. The English sentence The cat is on the mat and the Chinese sentence 「猫在垫子上」 look quite different yet express the same proposition, since they are true or false in exactly the same situations. A proposition is neither a sentence nor a speech event: one and the same sentence may express different propositions on different occasions, as with the indexical sentence 「我明天来」. Truth conditions are therefore the standard criterion of propositional identity."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "命题、语句与言语行为",
    "hEn": "Propositions, Sentences and Speech Acts",
    "p": [
     "语言哲学通常区分句子、命题与言语行为三个层次。句子是语言单位，命题是其承载的真值内容，言语行为则是说话人在具体语境中实施的断言、提问或命令。同一命题可以由陈述句、疑问句或名词化结构表达，例如「他离开了」「他离开了吗」「他的离开」。奥斯汀与塞尔由此把命题内容与言外之力分开处理，认为前者是共同的内容核心，后者决定话语的功能。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Philosophy of language commonly distinguishes three levels: the sentence, the proposition and the speech act. The sentence is a linguistic unit, the proposition is the truth-evaluable content it carries, and the speech act is the assertion, question or command performed by a speaker in context. The same proposition can be expressed by a declarative, an interrogative or a nominalisation, for instance 「他离开了」, 「他离开了吗」 and 「他的离开」. Austin and Searle accordingly separate propositional content from illocutionary force, treating the former as the shared core of content."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "命题态度与内涵语境",
    "hEn": "Propositional Attitudes and Intensional Contexts",
    "p": [
     "命题是命题态度动词的宾语。在 believe、know、doubt、hope 等动词之后，从句表达的不是事实，而是主体所持的态度内容。这类语境属于内涵语境：即使「启明星」与「长庚星」指称同一颗行星，替换之后仍可能改变真值。弗雷格因此提出涵义与指称之分，用以解释「启明星是长庚星」既有认知内容又只涉及同一个对象。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Propositions serve as the objects of propositional-attitude verbs. After verbs such as believe, know, doubt and hope, the embedded clause does not state a fact but reports the content of a mental attitude. Such contexts are intensional: even though 「启明星」 and 「长庚星」 refer to the same planet, substituting one for the other may change the truth value of the whole sentence. Frege therefore distinguished sense from reference in order to explain how 「启明星是长庚星」 is both informative and about a single object."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "争议与批评",
    "hEn": "Controversies and Criticisms",
    "p": [
     "命题的本体论地位长期存在争议。弗雷格视之为第三领域的抽象对象，罗素早期主张命题是包含对象与属性的复合体，蒯因则因其个体化困难而倾向以语句代替命题。结构化命题理论主张命题由对象、属性与结构组成，可能世界语义学则把命题等同于可能世界集合。这些理论之争直接影响着语义学处理态度归属与模态语境的方式。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "The ontological status of propositions remains disputed. Frege treated them as abstract objects belonging to a third realm; the early Russell held that they are complexes containing objects and properties; Quine, troubled by their individuation, preferred to speak of sentences instead. Structured-propositions theories analyse propositions as built from objects, properties and structure, whereas possible-worlds semantics identifies a proposition with a set of possible worlds. These disagreements bear directly on how semantics handles attitude attributions and modal contexts."
    ]
   }
  ],
