  "summary": "语义场指一组意义相关、相互制约的词在词汇系统中构成的聚合网络，又称词汇场。特雷尔等学者提出，词义并不孤立存在，而是在场内部通过彼此的分工与对立获得确定值，如汉语「父亲、母亲、儿子、女儿」构成亲属场。语义场理论把索绪尔的聚合关系落实到词汇层面，成为词汇语义学与义素分析的重要基础，后期又受到原型理论和框架语义学的修正。",
  "summaryEn": "A semantic field is a set of lexically related words that form a mutually defining network within the vocabulary, also called a lexical field. Trier and others argued that a word's meaning is not self-contained but emerges from the contrasts it contracts with its neighbours, as in the kinship field of father, mother, son, daughter or the colour field of red, orange and yellow. The theory applies Saussurean paradigmatic relations to lexis and underpins lexical semantics and componential analysis, though prototype theory and frame semantics have since qualified its claims.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": "定义",
    "hEn": "Definition",
    "p": [
     "语义场是词汇系统中一群在意义上相互关联、彼此制约的词所组成的聚合体。场内的词共享某个共同的语义区域，又通过各自的区别性特征划分这一区域。例如汉语的「兄、弟、姐、妹」同属亲属称谓场，其共同义素是「同胞」，区别义素则是「年长／年幼」与「男性／女性」。词义只有放到场中才获得完整的规定，离开场的对比便无法说明它究竟覆盖哪一段意义空间。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "A semantic field is a paradigmatically organised set of words whose meanings are related and mutually delimiting. Members of the field share a common semantic territory and divide it among themselves by distinctive features. In Chinese, for instance, xiong, di, jie and mei all belong to the kinship field of siblings: they share the component 'sibling' and differ by the components 'elder/younger' and 'male/female'. A word's value is fully specified only within the field, since outside its contrasts there is no way of saying which portion of meaning it covers."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "研究内容与理论来源",
    "hEn": "Subject Matter and Theoretical Sources",
    "p": [
     "语义场研究关注场的边界、场内词项的层级结构以及场与场之间的交叉。德国学者特雷尔在二十世纪三十年代通过对中古高地德语「智慧」类词汇的历时考察，证明同一意义区域在不同时代的切分方式会整体改变，从而把历时研究与词汇系统结合起来。波尔齐希则研究动词场，指出语法搭配同样参与词义的确定，如德语 treten 与 gehen 的差别在于是否涉及「地面接触」与「步态」。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Research on semantic fields concerns the boundaries of a field, the hierarchical structure of its members, and the overlap between fields. In the 1930s Jost Trier compared the Middle High German vocabulary of knowledge and showed that the way a conceptual area is partitioned changes as a whole over time, thereby linking diachronic study to the lexical system. Walter Porzig examined verb fields and argued that syntactic collocations also help fix meaning, as with the German verbs gehen and treten, which differ in whether contact with a surface and a stepping motion are involved."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "分类与示例",
    "hEn": "Types and Examples",
    "p": [
     "常见的场类型包括分类场、顺序场、关系场和联想场。分类场按上下义层级组织，如「花」下辖「玫瑰、郁金香」；顺序场按时间或程度排列，如「春、夏、秋、冬」；关系场依据对立，如「买／卖」；联想场依据心理联想，如由「医院」联想到「医生、护士」。英语颜色场 red、orange、yellow、green、blue 的边界与汉语颜色词并不完全重合，俄语更把英语 blue 分为 sinij 与 goluboj 两个基本词，说明场的切分具有语言相对性。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Common field types include taxonomic, sequential, relational and associative fields. Taxonomic fields are organised by hyponymy, as when flower subsumes rose, tulip and chrysanthemum; sequential fields order members by time or degree, as with spring, summer, autumn, winter or cold, warm, hot, scalding; relational fields rest on oppositeness, as with buy and sell or husband and wife; associative fields rest on psychological association, so hospital evokes doctor, nurse, bed and prescription. The English colour terms red, orange, yellow, green, blue and purple do not map neatly onto the Chinese set hong, cheng, huang, lü, lan, zi, and Russian splits the English blue region into the basic terms sinij and goluboj, showing that the partition of a field is language-specific."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "研究方法",
    "hEn": "Methods",
    "p": [
     "语义场分析通常从语料中提取候选词项，再通过替换与共现测试确定其归属，最后用义素矩阵描写场内差异。例如对汉语「看、望、瞧、盯、瞪」的分析可分解出「方向」「持续」「情绪」等义素。语料库工具可统计搭配与分布，词向量模型则通过余弦相似度自动聚出语义相近的词群，如 king 与 queen、man 与 woman 的向量差高度一致，但在场的边界判定上仍需语言学解释。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Semantic field analysis usually extracts candidate items from a corpus, tests their membership by substitution and co-occurrence, and then describes their differences with a componential matrix. Analyses of the Chinese visual verbs kan, wang, qiao, ding and deng, for instance, decompose them into features such as direction, duration and emotional stance. Corpus tools quantify collocation and distribution, and distributional word embeddings cluster semantically similar words automatically; the vector difference between king and queen closely matches that between man and woman. Deciding where a field ends nevertheless still requires linguistic interpretation."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "争议与批评",
    "hEn": "Controversies and Criticism",
    "p": [
     "批评者指出，场的边界往往依赖研究者的直觉，缺乏可操作的判定标准；把词义分解为离散义素也难以处理一词多义和模糊性。莱考夫与兰盖克等认知语言学家认为，词汇并非按清晰的特征矩阵组织，而是围绕原型辐射出多义网络。框架语义学主张以语义框架取代语义场，把词义与场景知识和句式联系起来。尽管如此，场的概念在词典编纂、同义词辨析和语言教学中仍被广泛使用。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Critics note that field boundaries often depend on the analyst's intuition and lack operational criteria, and that decomposing meaning into discrete components handles polysemy and vagueness poorly. Cognitive linguists such as Lakoff and Langacker argue that vocabulary is not organised by clear feature matrices but radiates from prototypes into polysemous networks. Frame semantics proposes replacing the field with the semantic frame, tying word meaning to scene knowledge and clause patterns. Even so, the notion of the field remains widely used in lexicography, synonym discrimination and language teaching."
    ]
   }
  ],
