  "summary": "预设指说话人视为理所当然、而非断言内容的背景信息。例如「张三不再抽烟了」预设「张三以前抽烟」，无论说成否定句还是疑问句，这一预设都保留。预设由特定触发语引起，如定指描述、事实动词、状态变化动词和分裂句。预设能否在否定、疑问、条件句等环境中存活，即所谓投射问题，是语义学与语用学长期争论的焦点，也是动态语义学的重要课题。",
  "summaryEn": "A presupposition is background information that a speaker takes for granted rather than asserts. 张三不再抽烟了 'Zhang San no longer smokes' presupposes that he used to smoke, and the presupposition survives under negation and questioning. Presuppositions are triggered by definite descriptions, factive verbs, change-of-state verbs and clefts, among others. Whether and how they project through negation, questions and conditionals is the projection problem, a central issue in semantics, pragmatics and dynamic semantics.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": "定义与否定测试",
    "hEn": "Definition and the Negation Test",
    "p": [
     "预设是话语中作为背景被预先假定为真的信息，区别于句子的断言内容。它最显著的特征是可以在否定、疑问、情态等环境下保持不变，即所谓「否定下的恒定」。英语 John stopped smoking 预设 John used to smoke，其否定 John didn't stop smoking 仍作同样预设。汉语亦然：「他后悔买了那辆车」与「他不后悔买了那辆车」都预设「他买了那辆车」。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "A presupposition is information taken for granted as background, as opposed to what a sentence asserts. Its hallmark is constancy under negation: it survives negation, questioning and modality. John stopped smoking presupposes that John used to smoke, and the negated John didn't stop smoking carries the same presupposition. Mandarin behaves alike, since 他后悔买了那辆车 and its negation 他不后悔买了那辆车 both presuppose that he bought the car."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "预设触发语",
    "hEn": "Presupposition Triggers",
    "p": [
     "预设通常由特定词语或句式引起，这些词语称为触发语。定指描述 the king of France 预设存在法国国王；事实动词 know、regret 预设其补语为真，「我知道他来了」预设「他来了」；状态变化动词 stop、begin 预设先前的状态；分裂句「是张三打破了窗户」预设「有人打破了窗户」。此外，again、too 和汉语「也」这样的重复义副词预设此前已存在同类事件。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Presuppositions are typically triggered by particular words and constructions. Definite descriptions such as the king of France presuppose existence; factive verbs like know and regret presuppose the truth of their complement, so 我知道他来了 presupposes that he came; change-of-state verbs like stop and begin presuppose a prior state; and clefts such as 是张三打破了窗户 presuppose that someone broke the window. Additives like again, too and 也 presuppose a prior or parallel event of the same kind."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "投射问题",
    "hEn": "The Projection Problem",
    "p": [
     "当预设出现在复合句中时，它是否保留由投射规律决定。在「如果张三停止抽烟，他的身体会好转」中，停烟预设依然投射出来；但在「如果张三曾经抽烟，那么他现在停止抽烟了」中，预设被条件句的前件吸收而不再出现。否定、情态和可能世界算子的性质决定预设能否穿透，这一现象称为投射问题，是坎普与斯托克纳克等人争论的核心。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "When a presupposition occurs inside a complex sentence, whether it survives is governed by projection rules. In 如果张三停止抽烟，他的身体会好转 the presupposition still projects, but in 如果张三曾经抽烟，那么他现在停止抽烟了 it is absorbed by the antecedent and disappears completely. The semantics of negation, modals and possible-world operators determines whether presuppositions penetrate, a phenomenon known as the projection problem and debated at length by Karttunen, Stalnaker and others."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "理论解释",
    "hEn": "Theoretical Accounts",
    "p": [
     "对预设存在语义学与语用学两类解释。语义预设理论把预设看作真值条件的一部分，预设失败会使句子既非真也非假，这可以解释「法国国王是秃头」的异常感。语用预设理论由斯托克纳克与格莱斯的传统发展而来，认为预设是说话人对共同背景的假定，属于言语行为的适切条件。当代动态语义学，如海姆的文件变更语义学，则用语境更新来统一解释预设的投射与适切性。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Accounts of presupposition fall into semantic and pragmatic families. Semantic theories treat presupposition as part of truth conditions, so that presupposition failure renders a sentence neither true nor false, which explains the oddity of The king of France is bald. Pragmatic theories, developing the tradition of Stalnaker and Grice, see presuppositions as speakers' assumptions about the common ground and as felicity conditions on speech acts. Dynamic semantics, such as Heim's file change semantics, models projection and felicity uniformly as context update."
    ]
   }
  ],
