  "summary": "基于用法的语言学主张语言知识来自语言使用，而非天赋的独立模块。它认为说话者借助固化、类比和范畴化等一般认知能力，从反复出现的语言经验中抽象出从具体词语到抽象构式的连续体，使用频率对单位的固化和提取起决定作用。兰盖克的认知语法、拜比的使用导向理论与托马塞洛的习得研究是其代表，研究常以语料库统计和心理语言学实验为证据。",
  "summaryEn": "Usage-based linguistics holds that linguistic knowledge emerges from language use rather than from an innate, domain-specific module. Speakers abstract a continuum of units, from concrete words to abstract constructions, out of repeated experience by means of general cognitive processes such as entrenchment, analogy and categorisation, with frequency playing a decisive role in storage and retrieval. Langacker's Cognitive Grammar, Bybee's usage-based theory and Tomasello's acquisition research are representative. Evidence typically comes from corpus statistics, psycholinguistic experiments and longitudinal child language data.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": "定义与核心主张",
    "hEn": "Definition and Central Claims",
    "p": [
     "基于用法的语言学是一组强调语言知识来源于语言使用的理论取向，与语言天赋论立场相对。其核心主张是：语法并非先天给定的独立模块，而是说话者在反复的语言经验中通过归纳、类比和范畴化逐步抽象出来的。语言单位从具体词语到抽象构式形成一个连续体，使用频率在其中起决定性作用：频率越高，单位越容易被固化和提取。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Usage-based linguistics is a family of approaches that treat linguistic knowledge as emerging from language use rather than from an innate, autonomous module. Its central claim is that grammar is abstracted by speakers from repeated experience through general cognitive processes such as entrenchment, analogy and categorisation. Linguistic units range along a continuum from concrete words to abstract constructions, and frequency plays a decisive role: the more often a pattern is used, the more strongly it is entrenched and the more easily it is retrieved."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "研究内容与方法",
    "hEn": "Research Questions and Methods",
    "p": [
     "基于用法的研究关注频率效应、构式网络、语法化、固化与能产性等问题，常用语料库统计、心理语言学实验和儿童语言追踪作为证据来源。例如英语中高频动词 give 与低频动词 donate 对双宾构式的支持程度明显不同，说明具体动词的频率塑造了论元结构的能产性。汉语「把」字句的扩展也显示，新用法总是从具体高频语境逐步泛化到更抽象的图式。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Research in this tradition addresses frequency effects, construction networks, grammaticalisation, entrenchment and productivity, and it draws evidence from corpus statistics, psycholinguistic experiments and longitudinal child data. A well-known example is the English dative alternation, where high-frequency verbs such as give support the double-object construction far more robustly than low-frequency verbs such as donate, showing that verb-specific frequency shapes argument-structure productivity. Similar evidence comes from the spread of the Chinese ba construction, whose new uses generalise from concrete, frequent contexts to more abstract schemas."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "理论渊源与发展",
    "hEn": "Intellectual Roots and Development",
    "p": [
     "该取向可追溯到二十世纪的功能主义传统以及博厄斯、萨丕尔的语言描写实践，也受到维果茨基社会文化理论的影响。二十世纪八十年代以后，兰盖克与莱考夫等人推动的认知语言学为其提供了理论框架，拜比、汤普森和托马塞洛等人则通过实证研究加以充实。近二十年来，大规模语料库与心理语言学实验的结合，使其成为与生成语法并立的重要范式。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "The approach traces its ancestry to twentieth-century functionalism, to the descriptive practice of Boas and Sapir, and to Vygotskian sociocultural theory. From the 1980s onward the cognitive linguistics of Langacker and Lakoff supplied its theoretical frame, while Bybee, Thompson and Tomasello enriched it with empirical work on phonology, syntax and acquisition. In the past two decades the combination of large corpora with psycholinguistic experimentation has established usage-based linguistics as a major paradigm standing alongside generative grammar."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "争议与批评",
    "hEn": "Controversies and Criticism",
    "p": [
     "批评主要来自生成语法阵营：反对者认为，仅凭输入频率和一般认知机制难以解释儿童在短时间内获得的抽象句法知识，也无法说明某些结构虽罕见却极易习得的现象。此外，频率效应的因果方向难以确定，语料库中的共现数据有时混入语用与文体因素。支持者回应说，抽象图式与频率并非互斥，两者可以在同一框架内共存。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Criticism comes mainly from the generative camp: opponents argue that input frequency and general cognitive mechanisms cannot explain how children acquire abstract syntax so rapidly, nor why some rare structures are learned with ease. The causal direction of frequency effects is also hard to establish, and corpus co-occurrence data may be confounded by pragmatic and stylistic factors. In reply, proponents maintain that abstract schemas and frequency are not mutually exclusive but can be integrated within a single framework."
    ]
   }
  ],
