  "summaryEn": "Experimental phonetics uses instruments and experimental methods to measure the physiological and acoustic properties of speech and to study how listeners perceive it. It supplements traditional impressionistic judgement with objective data, describing speech through parameters such as the spectrogram, fundamental frequency, formants and voice onset time. It is a key marker of the modernisation of phonetics and also serves speech recognition and language teaching."
