  "summary": "标音是用书写符号系统记录语言语音的方法，是语音学研究的基础技术。它把连续的语流切分为音段，用一套约定符号逐段记录，可分为以斜杠标示音位对立为主的宽式音位标音与放在方括号内、记录音位变体及细微语音细节的严式语音标音。国际音标是最通用的标音系统，其原则是每个符号只代表一个音，每个音只用一个符号。标音广泛用于语音学、方言学、语言教学、词典编纂和言语病理学。",
  "summaryEn": "Phonetic transcription is the practice of representing speech with a set of writing symbols, and it constitutes the basic descriptive technique of phonetics. Continuous speech is segmented into units and recorded with agreed symbols. Broad, phonemic transcription, conventionally placed between slashes, captures only contrasts that are linguistically significant, while narrow, phonetic transcription in square brackets also records allophonic and sub-phonemic detail. The International Phonetic Alphabet is the most widely used system, built on the principle of one symbol for one sound. Transcription serves phonetics, dialectology, language teaching, lexicography and speech pathology.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": "定义与基本性质",
    "hEn": "Definition and Basic Nature",
    "p": [
     "标音指用一套约定的书写符号把口语的语音记录下来，是使稍纵即逝的声音得以观察、比较和保存的技术手段。它依据听觉印象和声学分析，把连续语流切分为可以识别的音段单位，再为每个单位选定符号。标音的基本要求是可读、可比、可复现，即他人依据符号能够还原出大致相同的发音。由于任何符号系统都无法穷尽语音的连续细节，标音本质上是对语音的简化与抽象，标音的精细程度取决于研究目的，而非语音本身的属性。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Transcription is the technique of recording spoken language with an agreed set of writing symbols, making fleeting sounds observable, comparable and permanent. Working from auditory impressions and acoustic measurements, the transcriber segments continuous speech into identifiable units and assigns a symbol to each. Adequate transcription must be readable, comparable and reproducible: another analyst should be able to recover broadly the same pronunciation from the symbols. Because no notation can exhaust the continuous detail of speech, transcription is inherently a simplification or abstraction, and the degree of detail required depends on the analyst's purpose rather than on the nature of speech itself."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "宽式标音与严式标音",
    "hEn": "Broad and Narrow Transcription",
    "p": [
     "宽式标音又称音位标音，通常放在斜杠之间，只记录具有区别意义作用的音位，如英语 cat 记作 /kæt/。严式标音又称语音标音，通常放在方括号内，除音位对立外还记录音位变体和协同发音细节，如同一词可记作 [kʰæt] 或 [kʰæˀt]，其中的送气符号和喉塞音符号都表示附加信息。两者并非互相对立，而是同一连续体上的两端：标音者可在方括号内只写必要的细节，例如汉语普通话的妈可以只记调值 [ma˥]，也可以进一步标出声学上更细致的描写。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Broad transcription, also called phonemic transcription and conventionally enclosed in slashes, records only the phonemes that carry contrast, as in English cat /kæt/. Narrow transcription, or phonetic transcription, is written in square brackets and additionally marks allophones and coarticulatory detail: the same word may appear as [kʰæt] or [kʰæˀt], where the aspiration and glottalisation marks convey extra information. The two are not opposed categories but end points of one continuum, and an analyst may include only the detail that the argument requires, writing the Mandarin word for mother as [ma˥] or adding further acoustic specification as needed."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "标音系统与国际音标",
    "hEn": "Transcription Systems and the IPA",
    "p": [
     "十九世纪以来出现了多种标音系统，如转写英语方言的可见言语符号、派克式美国描写语言学标音法，以及为梵语等古典语言设计的转写方案。国际音标由国际语音学协会于 1888 年首次公布，是最通行的系统，其核心原则是一个符号对应一个音，一个音只用一个符号，符号资源包括肺气流辅音表、元音四边形图、非肺气流音和附加符号，如送气符号 ʰ、鼻化符号 ̃ 和声调字母 ˥ ˧ ˩。它还可借附加符号为未见过的语言临时扩展符号。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Several systems appeared from the nineteenth century onwards, including Visible Speech for English dialects, the American descriptivist tradition associated with Pike, and the transliteration schemes devised for classical languages such as Sanskrit. The International Phonetic Alphabet, first published by the International Phonetic Association in 1888, is now the dominant system. Its guiding principle is one symbol for one sound and one sound for one symbol. Its resources include a chart of pulmonic consonants, the vowel quadrilateral, non-pulmonic sounds and a set of diacritics such as ʰ for aspiration, ̃ for nasalisation, ˞ for rhoticity and ˥ ˧ ˩ for tone levels. A particular strength is that unseen sounds can often be notated by adding diacritics or modifier letters."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "示例与现代实践",
    "hEn": "Examples and Modern Practice",
    "p": [
     "严式标音能清楚显示普通话送气与不送气的对立：怕 [pʰa˥˩] 与爸 [pa˥˩] 只靠送气符号 ʰ 区别，而同样的差别在英语中只是同一音位的条件变体。法语 vin 记作 [vɛ̃]，鼻化符号显示元音带有鼻化；日语助词は 实际读作 [wa]，显示书写与读音分离。如今标音常与声学分析结合，在语音软件中标注音段边界、基频曲线和共振峰数据，并借助统一码与数据库实现检索复用。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Narrow transcription makes the Mandarin aspiration contrast transparent: the words for fear and father are [pʰa˥˩] and [pa˥˩], distinguished solely by the aspiration diacritic, whereas in English the same difference is allophonic, as in speak [spiːk] with unaspirated p and peak [pʰiːk] with aspirated p. French vin is transcribed [vɛ̃], the tilde marking nasality on the vowel, and the Japanese particle written ha is pronounced [wa], showing the gap between spelling and sound. In contemporary work transcription is combined with acoustic analysis, so that segment boundaries, fundamental frequency tracks and formant measurements are labelled in software and stored in Unicode-based searchable databases."
    ]
   }
  ],
