  "summaryEn": "Fieldwork is the method by which linguists go into a speech community and collect first-hand data by working with speakers and observing everyday interaction. It is the basic technique of descriptive linguistics, dialectology and endangered-language documentation, stressing the collection of material in natural contexts and the creation of durable language archives through IPA transcription and recording equipment."
