  "summaryEn": "Corpus linguistics is a methodological approach that studies language by means of computerised retrieval and statistics applied to large collections of authentic texts. It stresses the description of language use on the basis of verifiable frequency and contextual evidence, and is widely used in lexicography, grammar research, language teaching and natural language processing; representative resources include the BNC and COCA for English and the Modern Chinese corpus."
