  "summaryEn": "Elicitation is a survey method in which the researcher gets speakers to produce or judge particular linguistic forms through tasks such as questioning, picture naming and sentence substitution. It can cover phonological, lexical and grammatical categories systematically within a relatively short time, and is often combined with the collection of natural data; it is a standard technique in fieldwork and experimental linguistics."
