  "summaryEn": "The questionnaire survey is a quantitative method that puts standardised questions to respondents in written or electronic form in order to collect data systematically on language use, language attitudes and social background. It yields comparable data from relatively large samples and is often combined with sociolinguistic sampling designs to study language variation, bilingual usage and language policy."
