  "summaryEn": "H. P. Grice (1913–1988) was a British philosopher and linguist and a founder of ordinary language philosophy and of pragmatics. He distinguished natural from non-natural meaning, proposed the Cooperative Principle of conversation together with the maxims of Quantity, Quality, Relation and Manner, and on this basis built the theory of conversational implicature, deeply influencing pragmatics and the philosophy of language."
