   {
    "h": "语言实例与间接言语行为",
    "hEn": "Linguistic Examples and Indirect Speech Acts",
    "p": [
     "塞尔指出，同一命题内容可承载不同语力。英语中「约翰将离开」这一命题内容分别出现在断言 John will leave、指令 Will John leave? 与承诺 I promise that John will leave 之中，语力随句式与语境而变。",
     "间接言语行为是形式与语力不一致的现象。英语 Can you reach the salt? 以疑问形式行使请求，其成立依赖听话人对合作原则的推断；汉语「你能把盐递给我吗」同理。塞尔也用「我把书放在桌子上」这类句子说明命题内容与宣告力量可以分离。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Searle stressed that one propositional content may carry different forces. The proposition that John will leave appears in the assertive John will leave, the directive Will John leave? and the commissive I promise that John will leave, with the force varying according to sentence form, verb and context rather than being determined by the content alone. The distinction between sentence form and illocutionary force therefore became a central theme of later pragmatics.",
     "Indirect speech acts arise when form and force diverge. English Can you reach the salt? is interrogative in form but functions as a request, and its interpretation rests on Gricean reasoning about the speaker's intentions. The Chinese sentence 你能把盐递给我吗 works in exactly the same way, showing that sentence form and illocutionary force need not coincide in either language. The distinction between sentence form and illocutionary force therefore became a central theme of later pragmatics."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "心智哲学与社会实在",
    "hEn": "Philosophy of Mind and Social Reality",
    "p": [
     "1980年塞尔提出中文屋论证：一个不懂汉语的人按规则手册在屋内处理汉字符号，对外给出看似正确的回答，却并不理解汉语。他由此论证形式符号操作本身不足以产生语义理解，反对以程序实现心灵的主张。",
     "在《社会实在的建构》中，他把言语行为理论扩展到制度领域，提出X在语境C中算作Y的公式，并强调集体意向性与宣告式言语行为在创造货币、婚姻、所有权等制度事实中的作用。语言因此不只是描述世界的工具，也是建构社会事实的机制。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "In 1980 Searle proposed the Chinese room argument: a person who knows no Chinese manipulates symbols according to a rule book and returns apparently correct answers, yet understands nothing at all of what he is doing. He concluded that formal symbol manipulation alone cannot generate semantic understanding, which is his central objection to the claim that running a program produces a mind.",
     "In The Construction of Social Reality he extended speech act theory to institutions with the formula X counts as Y in context C, stressing collective intentionality and declarative speech acts in creating institutional facts such as money, marriage and property. Language therefore does not merely describe an independent world but actively helps to constitute social reality. His later books argue that institutional facts exist only because communities collectively recognise and maintain them."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "影响与批评",
    "hEn": "Influence and Criticism",
    "p": [
     "塞尔的语力分类至今仍是语用学教科书的通行框架，间接言语行为研究、礼貌理论与话语分析都从中受益；他关于心智与意识的研究亦推动了认知科学的哲学讨论，其著作被广泛译介并用于语言学教学。",
     "中文屋论证引发了持久的争论。批评者提出系统回复、机器人回复与模拟回复等反驳，认为理解可能属于整个系统而非屋内的人；塞尔则坚持句法不等于语义，计算只能给出模拟而非真正的意向性。也有学者质疑其分类在跨语言场景中的稳定性以及宣告类语力的界定标准。"
    ],
    "pEn": [
     "Searle's classification of illocutionary acts remains a standard framework in pragmatics textbooks, informing work on indirect speech acts, politeness theory and discourse analysis, while his writings on mind and consciousness contributed to philosophical debate in cognitive science and are widely translated for use in linguistics teaching around the world. The debate continues to shape discussions of artificial intelligence, consciousness and the limits of computation.",
     "The Chinese room has prompted sustained objections, including the systems, robot and simulation replies, which hold that understanding may belong to the whole system rather than to the person inside. Searle insists that syntax is not sufficient for semantics and that computation yields simulation rather than genuine intentionality; other critics question the cross-linguistic stability of his categories and the boundaries of declarations."
    ]
   }
