  "summaryEn": "M. A. K. Halliday (1925-2018) was a British linguist and the founder of systemic functional grammar. He held that language is a social semiotic system and that grammar consists of a meaning potential open to choice; he proposed the three metafunctions, ideational, interpersonal and textual, and applied linguistic research widely to language education, discourse analysis and translation studies."
